message: "If you use this model, its results or the paper, please cite the paper."
title: "Circulation-Priced Money: a holding charge that pays for pooled liquidity"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Totla
    given-names: Siddharth
date-released: "2026-11-22"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/cpm-research/circulation-priced-money"
abstract: >-
  An agent-based model of Circulation-Priced Money, a payment money whose holders pay a small holding charge
  (demurrage) that goes to one liquidity pool owned by its users, compared on the same simulated people with banks
  and cards, a best-case decentralised arrangement and the pool without the charge. The repository holds the model,
  the registered analysis plan, the tests that tie the paper's equations and parameters to the code, and the stored
  results the paper is rebuilt from.
keywords:
  - demurrage
  - holding charge
  - pooled liquidity
  - household credit
  - payments
  - decentralised finance
  - agent-based model
  - mechanism design
